     1	# RelayDesk
     2	
     3	RelayDesk is a small provider-neutral coordination service for background coding sessions. It collects concise context from concurrent work, returns a bounded brief to the next session, and can hard-block proposed work that contradicts certified architecture rules.
     4	
     5	This repository is intentionally small. The `internal/coordination` package owns the shared records, briefs, certified rule model, and deterministic admission policy. Ordinary decision records remain descriptive; only current rules with maintainer certification are executable.
     6	
     7	```bash
     8	go test ./...
     9	go run ./cmd/relaydesk
    10	```
    11	
    12	The command evaluates an intentionally contradictory example proposal. It prints a structured blocked evaluation and exits with status 1, demonstrating the hard admission boundary.
